----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `no authorized key was packed into the boot image` | the key was written after the image, or in a path the installed hook does not read | re-run `install`; the CLI asks the installed hook which path it reads rather than assuming |"],[1832,"| Report                                             | Cause                                  | Fix                                              |\n| -------------------------------------------------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |\n| `an encrypted /boot needs GRUB to read the initrd` | `/boot` is inside the encrypted volume | verify GRUB can read it before trusting a reboot |"],[1824,"| Report                                             | Cause                  | Fix                                                                                               |\n| -------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `no initramfs address (IP is unset, none, or off)` | nothing ever set `IP=` | `install --ip dhcp`, or `--iface ens3` to pin one NIC, or a raw netboot spec for a static network |"],[1830,"| Report                                            | Cause                                                              | Fix                                                                             |\n| ------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| `MODULES=dep packs only drivers loaded right now` | the NIC driver is not loaded today, so it will be missing tomorrow | name the driver in `/etc/initramfs-tools/modules`, or go back to `MODULES=most` |"],[1826,"| Report                            